2026-09-14 [REJECTED] early stopping of comparison runs, for now — Full; the human chose to defer it on the analyst's findings. A stop that certifies the full-run verdict never fires after run 1 (the remaining runs can always flip it) and, by the analyst's search, not before task 21 of 27 even on the broken e20; the safe variant, early REJECT only at a strict target, would have stopped e20 after 18 tasks (35.5% of its input tokens) but saves nothing on a PASS, and 12 of the 17 judgeable stored comparisons are PASSes; an early PASS is a loosening whose miss rate cannot be measured before the sensitivity epoch. Next: the within-task (stratified) test; stopping, if ever, is built on top of it.
2026-09-14 [REJECTED] a within-task (stratified) statistic for the acceptance rule — Full; the human chose to keep the rule on the analyst's finding, re-derived by hand: with 2 scored runs per arm in every task and the cut taken from the epoch's own permutation null, each dimension's stratified z is its pooled z divided by a constant for that dimension, so per dimension it is the same test. It only reweights dimensions inside the worst-of minimum (more weight to the rarely varying outcome and gate_ran, less to consent and writes; by the analyst's replay e19's cut would move from -2.32 to -2.45), no stored verdict would change, and no gain can be shown without an invented break. The 2026-09-13 assessment that it sees a moderate drop better does not hold for this design. If the sensitivity epoch runs, both statistics are compared offline on its scores; the entry above that builds any future stopping "on top of" the stratified test is void — it would sit on the current rule.
